.TH FEIGEN 3 "2026-10-12" "feigen 0.1.0" "Fortran Library Functions"
.SH NAME
feigen \- stiffness eigenmodes of a single finite element, named and plotted
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B use cubatures
.B use shapefuncs
.B use feigen
.B D = material(dim, E, nu)
.B K = stiffness(s, q, X, D)
.B call modes(K, lambda, phi [, tol])
.B call name_modes(X, lambda, phi, names, match [, tol])
.B call plot_modes(s, X, lambda, phi, names, scale, filename)
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Module
.B feigen
computes the stiffness matrix of one isotropic linear elastic finite element,
its eigenvalues and eigenvectors, names the modes and plots them. The element
is a
.B shapefunc
s from fortran_shapefuncs at the points of a
.B cubature
q from fortran_cubatures, with nodal coordinates X(dim, nnodes). Values are
real64. Degrees of freedom are ordered node by node.
.SS Procedures
.TP
.BR material ( dim ", " E ", " nu )
Elasticity matrix in Voigt notation with engineering shear strains, order xx,
yy, zz, xy, xz, yz: a bar in 1D, plane strain in 2D. Pure.
.TP
.BR stiffness ( s ", " q ", " X ", " D )
K = sum over points of B^T D B det(J) w, size dim*nnodes.
.TP
.BR "call modes" ( K ", " lambda ", " phi " [, " tol ])
Ascending eigenvalues and orthonormal eigenvectors of symmetric K. Eigenvalues
below tol*max|lambda| (default 1e-10) are set to exactly zero.
.TP
.BR "call name_modes" ( X ", " lambda ", " phi ", " names ", " match " [, " tol ])
Within each group of equal eigenvalues (default tol 1e-8), replace the
eigenvectors by the projections of the best-matching named fields: translation,
rotation, expansion, tension/compression, shear, bending, torsion, warping,
hourglass. match is the cosine between field and eigenspace. Modes without a
match are named "-". The catalog covers linear line, quadrilateral and
hexahedral elements.
.TP
.BR "call plot_modes" ( s ", " X ", " lambda ", " phi ", " names ", " scale ", " filename )
One PNG, SVG or PDF, chosen by the extension, with a subplot per mode. The
largest displacement is scale times the element size.
.SS Program
The
.B feigen
program wraps the module in a command line; see
.BR "feigen --help" .
.SH NOTES
.B feigen
does not check its arguments. Invalid elements and orders stop the program in
fortran_cubatures or fortran_shapefuncs with
.BR "error stop" ,
and a singular Jacobian stops it in stdlib. Errors cannot be caught.
.PP
Kinds are not exported; use real64 from iso_fortran_env. The module has no
state.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
type(cubature) :: q
type(shapefunc) :: s
real(dp) :: K(8,8), lambda(8), phi(8,8)
q = cubature(CUB_QUA, 1)             ! one point: reduced integration
s = shapefunc(q, 1)                  ! 4-node quadrilateral
K = stiffness(s, q, s%coords, material(2, 1._dp, 0.3_dp))
call modes(K, lambda, phi)
print *, count(lambda == 0)          ! 5: 3 rigid-body + 2 hourglass
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
The complete reference is llms.txt in the source distribution and
https://willklausler.github.io/feigen/
.SH AUTHOR
Will Klausler
